<section class="section">
    <div class="container legal-prose">
        <p>
            Tidy but Mighty Cleaning Service (&ldquo;we,&rdquo; &ldquo;our,&rdquo; or &ldquo;us&rdquo;) respects your privacy and is committed to protecting the personal information you share when visiting <strong>tidybutmightycleaning.com</strong> or booking cleaning services with us in Tennessee and Georgia.
        </p>

        <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Contact &amp; Estimate Details:</strong> Name, phone number, email address, city/service address, property details, and scheduling preferences submitted through our estimate form, email, phone, or SMS.</li>
            <li><strong>Service &amp; Billing Records:</strong> Appointment history, service checklists, invoices, and payment confirmation details.</li>
            <li><strong>Technical &amp; Usage Data:</strong> Standard browser, device, and diagnostic data (such as local storage or essential cookies used for Progressive Web App caching and form reliability).</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>2. How We Use Your Information</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>To provide accurate cleaning estimates, schedule appointments, and deliver residential or commercial cleaning services.</li>
            <li>To send appointment confirmations, arrival updates, receipts, and responses to your inquiries via email, phone, or SMS.</li>
            <li>To process payments, prevent fraud, and comply with applicable Tennessee, Georgia, and federal laws.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>3. Payment Processing (PCI-DSS Compliance)</h2>
        <p>
            If you pay for services electronically, payments are processed through trusted, PCI-DSS compliant third-party payment processors (such as <strong>Stripe</strong>, <strong>Square</strong>, or <strong>PayPal</strong>). We do <strong>not</strong> store full credit card numbers, CVV codes, or bank account credentials on our website servers. Your payment details are transmitted directly to and governed by the respective payment processor&rsquo;s security and privacy policies.
        </p>

        <h2>4. Third-Party Services &amp; Communications</h2>
        <p>
            We may use reputable third-party tools for website hosting (Microsoft Azure Static Web Apps), transactional email delivery, SMS/phone communications, and embedded map or social links (such as Facebook). We never sell, rent, or trade your personal information to third-party marketers.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Cookies &amp; Local Storage</h2>
        <p>
            This site operates as a Progressive Web App (PWA) and uses essential browser storage/service-worker caching to improve load speed and offline reliability. You can clear or disable cookies and site storage anytime through your browser settings.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Your Privacy Rights &amp; Data Requests</h2>
        <p>
            You may request access to, correction of, or deletion of your personal contact information at any time, or opt out of SMS/email communications by contacting us directly:
